## tick 4 env probe (post-commit): python-flint 0.9 Arb API for track B
machine said (verbatim):
  $ python3 -c "from flint.types.acb import acb; ..."
  zeta(1/2+12.9113i) = [0.49367026943924934909962 +/- 4.52e-24] +
                      [-0.68219025933531303105067 +/- 8.46e-25]j
api notes (verified, not from memory):
  - flint.ctx.prec = N sets midpoint precision (bits); flint.arb(mid, rad) —
    the 2nd constructor arg is the RADIUS, not precision (arb(1.4, 53) is the
    interval [1.4-53, 1.4+53]).
  - real balls: flint.arb; complex balls: from flint.types.acb import acb;
    acb(re, im) constructor.
  - complex zeta: acb.zeta(z) — works at ctx precision, returns acb with
    explicit radius. Also available: acb.zeta_zero, acb.zeta_zeros,
    dirichlet_eta, dirichlet_l; real side: flint.arb.zeta, flint.arb.zeta_nzeros,
    gamma/lgamma/digamma in the flint.arb function module.

